  "notes": "Eight of 39 YAML candidates are fixture-first on this stack; 31 remain unimplemented. NWS context uses the existing proposed Atmosphere source record rather than duplicating a source descriptor. Its role/rights/sensitivity/admission and cross-domain use remain unresolved; NOAA family settings do not admit it. The existing NOAA product role for NWS is regulatory context, not observed hazard truth. Only supplied HTTP-200 Kansas active-surface collections within 256 KiB/64 features are supported; non-200 and unbound 304s are refused. Private source snapshots retain instructions without surfacing them as fields or CLI content. Partial captures and zero messages never establish complete coverage or hazard absence. No source retrieval, next-page following, polling, notification, lifecycle write, persistence, geometry qualification, EvidenceBundle closure, release or deployment. Current Hazards indexes reconcile earlier stale placeholder statements while retaining their historical inspections. Accepted ADR-0029 reference supports repository placement/authority boundaries only, not data-policy, source, cross-domain ownership or public-use approval. Prior receipts and source records are unchanged. Main-targeted PR must follow TIGER PR 5966; no intermediate-base PR. Git CLI write auth remains unavailable; publish exact verified blobs/tree through the connected app."
